# ============================================
# UNDERSTANDING BEZIER CURVES
# ============================================
# bezier = name, x1, y1, x2, y2
#
# (x1, y1) = Start control point (acceleration)
# (x2, y2) = End control point (deceleration)
#
# Common patterns:
# - Ease out:  0.16, 1, 0.3, 1      (fast start, slow end)
# - Ease in:   0.7, 0, 0.84, 0      (slow start, fast end)
# - Linear:    1, 1, 1, 1            (constant speed)
# - Overshot:  0.05, 0.9, 0.1, 1.1  (bounces past then settles)
# - Spring:    0.68, -0.55, 0.265, 1.55 (bouncy spring effect)


# ============================================
# ANIMATION PARAMETERS EXPLAINED
# ============================================
# animation = NAME, ENABLED, DURATION, CURVE, STYLE
#
# NAME options:
#   - windows, windowsIn, windowsOut, windowsMove
#   - workspaces, specialWorkspace
#   - fade, fadeDim, fadeSwitch, fadeShadow, fadeIn
#   - border, borderangle
#
# ENABLED: 0 = off, 1 = on
#
# DURATION: Time in deciseconds (10 = 1 second)
#   - 1-3:   Very fast/snappy
#   - 4-7:   Smooth/balanced
#   - 8-15:  Slow/cinematic
#
# STYLE options:
#   - slide      (default sliding)
#   - slidevert  (vertical slide)
#   - popin X%   (scale from X% size)
#   - fade       (opacity transition)
#
# CURVE: Your bezier curve name or 'default'


